<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint Peter Port</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as St Peter Port</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint Peter Port is the capital and main harbour of Guernsey in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/channel-islands">Channel Islands</a>. A trading port since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, it was guarded by Castle Cornet on an islet in its harbour, and it prospered in the 18th century from privateering and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/entrepot">entrepôt</a> trade in wine and spirits. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-hugo">Victor Hugo</a> lived in exile at Hauteville House in the town, where he completed Les Misérables.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-peter-port.jpg" alt="Saint Peter Port" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Man vyi · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alb%C3%A8rt_%C3%89glyise_Saint_Pi%C3%A8rre_Port_Dg%C3%A8rn%C3%A9sy.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
